// Section 161 — Allowance of deductions. Stage 1 (IRC-06).
//
// "In computing taxable income under section 63, there shall be allowed as
// deductions the items specified in this part, subject to the exceptions
// provided in part IX (relating to items not deductible)." This is a
// STRUCTURAL/DEFINITIONAL provision: it does not itself allow or compute any
// deduction — it names part VI (§§161-198) as the SOURCE of the deduction
// items subject to part IX's (§§261-291) exceptions. No self-executing rule
// follows from the text alone.
//
// classification = NON_NORMATIVE (reason: "introduces the deductions
// allowed by this part, subject to the exceptions of part IX; states no
// computable rule of its own"). Recorded in the coverage row; the statutory
// note (26/161/note/4/1, a `transition` disposition) is likewise
// NON_NORMATIVE — a historical effective-date note for a repealed cross
// reference, not a rule in force.
